# Server-wide invariants (joinUp)

These span multiple `server/` subdirectories (routes, services, workers, sockets), which is why
they don't fit one narrower `.mdc` glob — but they're still server-only, so they don't belong in
`00-core-invariants.mdc` (that file loads for every task in the repo, including pure `next_app`/
`mobile_app` UI work that never touches this code).

## Auth & security
- Chat write paths must use `authenticateToken` / `socket.userId` + `checkChatPermission`.
- Never trust a client-supplied `userId`. Never fail-open a socket JWT check. Never leave
  `POST /api/messages` public.
- `req.user.isAdmin` comes from Clerk metadata (`isAdmin` / `role=admin`) or `ADMIN_USER_IDS`. Do not
  hardcode `false` (or `true`).

## Transactions
- Roster joins, waitlist promotion, and game creation must be atomic.
- Game + group chat pairing must happen in the same interactive transaction, where the group chat
  `id` exactly equals the `game.id`.

## Prisma client lifecycle
- Import `prisma` from `server/lib/prisma.js`. Never instantiate `new PrismaClient()` inside an
  Express request handler, a loop, or a worker tick (one client per process). This one isn't
  Jest-testable in the normal behavioral sense — it's enforced by `npm run check:prisma-singleton`
  (`scripts/check-single-prisma-client.mjs`) instead, a static scan with the same one-off-CLI-script
  exception documented in `prisma-db.mdc`.

## Background job idempotency
- Scheduler handlers must claim work with `updateMany` on sentinel fields (`lotteryExecutedAt`,
  `reminderSent`, `pickingOpenedAt`, `status`) so a second instance is a no-op, **and re-read the
  row and check the due timestamp first**: a stale in-memory timer (row edited to a later time,
  schedule owned by another process) must never run a lottery/pick draw early. Anything non-claimed
  (review queue, series generation) must be a compare-and-set or sit behind a DB unique constraint.
- Exactly one process runs jobs: either `RUN_BACKGROUND_JOBS=false` on every extra instance, or
  `JOBS_LEADER_LOCK=redis` so only the Redis lock holder does (`services/leaderLock.js`; see
  `server/docs/agents/realtime_rules.md`). A deposed leader must call `gameScheduler.stop()`.

## Payments
- `Game.price` / `GameSeries.price` are display-only (pay at field). Do not add a payment processor
  without a product brief.
